  "description": "HOYRIA crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C264 H216 Co8 N16 O72 Pr8 S16,8(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Pr5 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr6 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Pr7 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr8 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co7 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co8 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.535-4.021 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.29-112.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni8Pr8(μ3-OH)n(mmt)8(Hdpga)x(CH3COO)y]·8CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
  "article_compound": {
